{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 25, :comments ["<b>And they sat to eat bread.</b> An expression of tarrying and settling: they settled themselves for the meal." "<b>And in the Midrash</b> of Tehillim: ״וישבו לאכול לחם״ — the Holy One, blessed be He, said: You sold your brother in the midst of eating and drinking, as it says, ״וישבו לאכול לחם״; behold, your children are sold in Shushan in the midst of eating and drinking, as it says (Esther 1:3) ״בשנת שלש למלכו״ and so forth; and Haman comes and takes you in the midst of eating and drinking, as it says (ibid. 3) ״והמלך והמן ישבו לשתות״ and so forth."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:20.737580993Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}